# 023a FR-003 — the maintenance loop's schedule kicker, EXAMPLE COPY.
#
# This file is a sample on purpose: the loader (src/sdlc/schedules/loader.py)
# globs `*.yaml`, so the `.yaml.sample` suffix keeps it OUT of every apply
# run — `sdlc schedules list` must only ever show real assets. To schedule a
# project's maintenance cycle, copy this file to `schedules/maint-<project>.yaml`,
# set `project` below, then run `python -m sdlc.cli schedules apply --dry-run`.
#
# The kicker wakes the project's MaintenanceWorkflow at cadence; one cycle
# runs per nudge (R2 coalescing), so an hourly-or-slower cron is enforced at
# load time for kick assets — the cycle is probe-dominated and cannot run
# faster anyway (see schedules/models.py).
spec:
  cron: "0 4 * * *"
  timezone: UTC
action:
  workflow: MaintenanceKickWorkflow
  project: demo
